  "scope": "Every randomized compatibility sweep, its variants regenerated from each record's generator, with the 2026-10-06 multi-target references, censuses and sweeps and the production gear swaps, compared again after moving the reference pin from 2d93e423e to 041dec8ef (the fork's merge of community #720 to #763 and its patches 100 to 112, client 70338). The rerun also takes in the 17 records the earlier pin reruns left out: the Warrior prepull sweep, the two rotation unit records, the 2026-10-05 multi-target references, the four tanking records against several targets and the nine 2026-10-08 sweeps. All 14,341 variants of the 124 records were compared: 14,278 match Go, Rust refuses 63 and none differ. Of the 9,076 variants of the 107 records the 2d93e423e rerun covered, 9,064 match and Rust refuses 12, the 12 Mage census presets the pin rewrote; of the 5,265 variants of the other 17, 5,214 match and Rust refuses 51, as their records did or fewer.",
  "generator": "each record's generator, at its seed; the variants a record keeps are compared as they are; the production gear swaps by their record's generate.py at 50 iterations; a generator that reads every accepted fixture (tools/rotation_forms.py casts, tools/copy_targets.py) is kept to the requests its record lists",
  "rerun": "python3 tools/prepared_v2.py compare --output <scratch> <variants>/*.json for each record",
  "criteria": {
    "comparison": "full RaidSimResult except elapsedNs, lists keyed by ID",
    "integer_counts": "exact",
    "floats": "relative 1e-9",
    "deviations": "as variances at the scale of mean^2",
    "first_fight_debug_log": "line identical"
  },
  "matched": 14278,
  "rejected": 63,
  "mismatched": 0,
  "errors": 0,
  "not_compared": 0,
  "request_digests": "every variant compared but 16 is the request its record lists: 11,338 by the prepared request_sha256, the 48 of the 2026-10-03 Fire and Arcane sweeps by the request file's SHA-256, and the 2,939 production gear swaps, whose record lists no digest, by count and scenario name. The 16 are the preset variants of the 2026-10-06 Mage census, which the generator reads from the pinned reference's presets: at 041dec8ef the Arcane, Fire and Frost presets read unitDistance and run prepull actions, which Rust refuses, so 12 of the 16 are refused and the 4 fire_lowrank variants match. The gear swap generator reads the pinned item database, which the pin moved to client 70338, and still gives the same 2,939 swaps by name. tools/rotation_forms.py casts and tools/copy_targets.py now also write 46 and 116 requests from fixtures accepted after their records; those were not compared.",
  "retries": "four variants whose export or Go run timed out at 300 seconds under the machine's load were compared again on their own and match: two of the item sweep and two of the tank fixture sweep. Five chunks of the tank fixture sweep ran while the worktree's build directory was being rebuilt, found no Rust binary or timed out waiting for it, and were compared again once it was built",
  "regeneration": "387 variants of four records (the in-front Enhancement base of the multi-target Shaman sweep, the tank fixture sweep, the tank sweep and the near Marksmanship Hunter base of the melee weapon proc sweep) were first drawn without the record's --max-distance 5, which keeps every field the records list but the distance; they matched Go as well. They were drawn again at the record's distance, compared, and those are the variants counted, each with its record's request digest",
  "reference_changes": {
    "compared": "the Go goldens of the accepted fixtures with goldens, the full RaidSimResult and the first-fight log, at 2d93e423e and at 041dec8ef",
    "moved": "256 of the 584 Go goldens changed, 217 of them in DPS; see UPSTREAM.md",
    "not_compared": "Go at the old pin was not run on the sweep variants; the comparison that counts is the new Go against Rust"
  },
